 ],
 "narrative": [
  "All courses taken to satisfy major requirements must be taken for a letter grade, and only grades of C– or better will be accepted in the visual arts major.",
  "A minimum of two-thirds of the course work completed for the major must be taken at UC San Diego.",
  "Double majors within the department (art history/theory/criticism paired with studio, speculative design, media, or ICAM) must have at least ten upper-division courses that are unique to each departmental major.",
  "Degree: the Music page says the department offers 'a bachelor of arts in music, music humanities, and ICAM'.",
  "The interdisciplinary computing and the arts major is in the Departments of Music and Visual Arts.",
  "Overlapping courses may be taken for the intermediate or advanced level, but not both.",
  "The Music page (catalog.ucsd.edu/curric/MUS-ug.html) also describes ICAM, with an older-looking list (VIS 41 and MUS 4/6/7/13/14, math MATH 20A-B or 10A-B-C or 15A or CSE 20, CSE 11 or VIS 42, four quarters of MUS 43 or VIS 10, three of MUS 170, 171, VIS 142, 145A, practice/advanced practice/theory electives, senior project MUS 160A-B); this file follows the Visual Arts page, which gives the major code VA29."
 ]
}